---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { musicEnabled, site } from "../data/site";
---

<Base title="Privacy policy | Digvijay Rathore" description="How digvijay.online handles personal data.">
  <article class="case legal">
    <a class="back" href="/">← Index</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Datenschutzerklärung</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="hook">Short version: no cookies, no ad tracking, no session recordings. This page explains the rest.</p>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Digvijay Singh Rathore<br />
      Franz-Jacob-Str. 3, 10369 Berlin, Germany<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Ave #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA. When you open a page, Vercel
      processes technical data that your browser sends automatically: IP address, date and time, the page requested,
      browser type and operating system. This is needed to deliver the site and keep it secure.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in running a stable and secure website). Data may be processed
      in the USA; Vercel relies on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      I use PostHog (PostHog Inc., 2261 Market Street #4008, San Francisco, CA 94114, USA) to understand which pages are
      visited and where visitors come from. It runs in cookieless mode:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies are set and nothing is stored in your browser.</li>
      <li>No session recordings, no heatmaps and no advertising profiles.</li>
      <li>
        To count visits, PostHog's servers compute a hash from your IP address and browser type, using a secret value
        that is replaced every day. Visits therefore cannot be linked across days or traced back to you. I have set
        PostHog to discard IP addresses instead of storing them with the data.
      </li>
      <li>
        I see aggregate numbers: pages viewed, referring site, country, device type, and clicks on buttons such as
        "Book a call".
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in measuring reach and improving the site). Analytics data is
      processed on PostHog servers in the USA, on the basis of a data processing agreement that includes the EU
      standard contractual clauses. You can object at any time by writing to the email address above.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contacting me</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me, I process the data you send (your address and the content of your message) to reply to you. Legal
      basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, or Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your message is about a job or a contract. I delete messages when
      they are no longer needed. My mailbox is provided by Google (Gmail), so Google processes these emails on my behalf.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Links to other services</h2>
    <p>
      "Book a call" opens Cal.com. LinkedIn and GitHub links open those platforms. Once you follow a link, the privacy
      policy of that service applies. This site does not embed their scripts, so they receive no data until you click.
    </p>

    <h2>{musicEnabled ? "6. Fonts, media and the music player" : "6. Fonts and media"}</h2>
    <p>Fonts, images and videos are served from this site itself. Nothing is loaded from Google Fonts or video platforms.</p>
    {
      musicEnabled && (
        <p>
          The home page has an optional music button. Nothing is loaded until you press it. When you do, a player from
          Spotify (Spotify AB, Regeringsgatan 19, 111 53 Stockholm, Sweden) is loaded, and Spotify receives your IP address
          and may set its own cookies, as described in Spotify's privacy policy. Legal basis: your consent, given by
          pressing play (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). If you do not press the button, no data goes to Spotify.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the data I hold about you (Art. 15),</li>
      <li>have it corrected (Art. 16) or deleted (Art. 17),</li>
      <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18) and receive it in a portable format (Art. 20),</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21),</li>
      <li>
        complain to a supervisory authority, for example the Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und
        Informationsfreiheit.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Storage period and automated decisions</h2>
    <p>
      I keep personal data only for as long as the purposes above require. You are not obliged to provide any data to
      use this site, and I do not use automated decision-making or profiling.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes</h2>
    <p>I update this page when the site changes. Last updated: November 2026.</p>

    <p class="legal-foot"><a class="back" href="/impressum">Impressum →</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
